WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.000
BUILD 049. A PREFERENCE IS NOT A PERMANENT TRAIT. What helps or overwhelms a person can change with setting, goal, health, energy, company, timing, access, and prior response.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:06.000
BUILD PRIVATE CONTEXT. PREFERENCE · SENSITIVITY · GOAL · RESPONSE. Use synthetic browser-local records. Collect only what the person chooses, name purpose and expiry, preserve source and uncertainty, and offer correction, deletion, and export.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
KEEP CONTEXT ATTACHED. SETTING · TIME · SUPPORT · CONSTRAINT. Bind each response to the conditions in which it occurred. Keep contradictions, unknowns, changes, and one-off experiences instead of flattening them into a fixed profile.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.000
CHANGE THE MOMENT. REORGANIZE—DO NOT DIAGNOSE. When setting, goals, sensitivities, or responses change, reorder the visible constellation without inferring identity, disability, health status, intent, or what will work next.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.000
PRESERVE HUMAN CONTROL. VIEW · CORRECT · WITHDRAW · EXIT. Let the person inspect every field, restrict reuse and sharing, revoke consent, delete local state, carry a portable record, and choose no recommendation.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:18.000
SAVE THIS. CONTEXT BELONGS TO THE PERSON. PERSONAL CONTEXT BECOMES USEFUL WHEN IT STAYS PRIVATE, CORRECTABLE, SITUATIONAL, AND OWNED BY THE PERSON IT DESCRIBES.

